WEBVTT

00:00:00.242 --> 00:00:01.492
- Previously on The O.C.:
- Daddy!

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.992
Her dad beat up
my dad at my debutante ball.

00:00:04.492 --> 00:00:05.658
You can't blame Holly for that.

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:06.992
- I know Jimmy.
- I've heard.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.075
He still has your prom photo on our wall.

00:00:09.283 --> 00:00:10.867
- What do you want from me?
- I want a divorce.

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:13.033
I never should have broken up
with you in the first place.

00:00:13.242 --> 00:00:15.700
- I don't know what I should do.
- Let me know when you decide.

00:00:15.908 --> 00:00:18.867
You chose Luke, huh?
Chino didn't stand a chance.

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:25.033
Let's go.

00:00:28.242 --> 00:00:29.408
You're too late.

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.408
- The plan is undeniable.
- I'm denying it.

00:00:34.617 --> 00:00:36.325
We have my mom's Range Rover.

00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:39.908
We have a perfect alibi, as I go to
this comic-book convention every year.

00:00:40.117 --> 00:00:42.367
We have my entire life
of never doing anything wrong...

00:00:42.575 --> 00:00:44.825
...which lulls my parents
into a false sense of trust.

00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:49.492
And you wanna throw all that away for
Summer in a wet T-shirt doing body shots?

00:00:50.867 --> 00:00:53.533
I'm sorry. I thought that was
a rhetorical question. Yes...

00:00:53.742 --> 00:00:57.325
...Ryan, yes. On the last weekend
before school, one goes to Tijuana.

00:00:57.533 --> 00:00:59.908
It is tradition,
and it is a rite of passage.

00:01:00.117 --> 00:01:02.367
What happens in Mexico
stays in Mexico.

00:01:02.867 --> 00:01:04.242
What happens in Mexico?

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:07.033
I don't know. It stays there.
That's why we must go.

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:09.742
I don't know about lying
to your parents.

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.908
I can respect that. I will lie to them.

00:01:13.367 --> 00:01:15.242
Why can't we just go to Comicon?

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.325
Comicon is a bunch
of pathetic virgins...

00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:19.658
...ogling some porn star dressed
as Catwoman.

00:01:19.867 --> 00:01:21.867
I thought you went every year.

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:26.492
Listen. Tijuana's a big town.
I'm sure you won't even see Marissa.

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:29.742
I don't care about seeing Marissa
or not seeing Marissa.

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:32.950
Therefore, you should have
no problem coming to Mexico, right?

00:01:33.158 --> 00:01:35.200
Well, won't she be hanging out
with Summer?

00:01:35.408 --> 00:01:37.367
No, she'll probably be
shacked up with Luke.

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.200
Yeah, I'm sorry.
That was probably a bit painful.

00:01:41.408 --> 00:01:43.950
Hey, fellas.
You all excited about Comicon?

00:01:44.158 --> 00:01:47.908
Seth's been going since he was 10.
It's the highlight of his year.

00:01:48.117 --> 00:01:50.783
Thanks. "Highlight" is a bit overstating it.

00:01:50.992 --> 00:01:55.367
- Check you out. Big pimping.
- I got a meeting with a private law firm.

00:01:55.575 --> 00:01:58.075
- You suing one of their clients?
- It's a job interview.

00:01:58.283 --> 00:02:02.033
Which he'll never take. They like to
flatter him every once in a while.

00:02:02.242 --> 00:02:06.742
- Yeah, I go for the free meal.
- But you'll still be a public defender, right?

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:10.033
After 15 years?
There's no way he's selling out.

00:02:10.242 --> 00:02:12.408
Well, it'd have to be
one hell of a free meal.

00:02:12.617 --> 00:02:15.158
And that's what's they call
a "callback" in comedy.

00:02:15.367 --> 00:02:17.825
So how soon until you two
are leaving on your trip?

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:19.742
I don't know. How soon?

00:02:23.242 --> 00:02:24.617
Tomorrow.

00:02:26.283 --> 00:02:28.367
Don't you mean "ma Íana"?

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.533
- Looks good.
- I don't wear hats.

00:03:09.908 --> 00:03:11.700
Ryan, you mean "sombrero."

00:03:11.867 --> 00:03:15.325
Brush up on your Spanish.
There's over 500 useful phrases.

00:03:18.283 --> 00:03:22.658
"May I please see a ladies' worsted
nylon bathing suit?"

00:03:22.825 --> 00:03:25.117
Yeah. Well, did you know that one?

00:03:25.325 --> 00:03:28.283
- What's this?
- An itinerary for our trip.

00:03:28.492 --> 00:03:30.783
Seth, it's 12 pages long.
We're going for two days.

00:03:30.992 --> 00:03:33.492
If you're gonna get over Marissa,
you need activities.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:36.450
I don't need to get over Marissa.
I'm over Marissa.

00:03:37.533 --> 00:03:40.367
Ryan. Ryan.

00:03:40.533 --> 00:03:44.242
Look at me.
Look, this is me here, okay? Amigo.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:48.242
Now, I know you're hurting, and I think
you need to unburden your soul.

00:03:51.658 --> 00:03:55.992
- Any time. I'm here to help.
- My soul is fine. Marissa and me...

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:59.617
It just... I don't know.
It never would have worked.

00:03:59.825 --> 00:04:02.325
No kidding.
It is so much better this way.

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:05.617
He's all, like, brooding, wounded,
"Somebody save me."

00:04:05.825 --> 00:04:09.283
- I thought you liked that.
- It is too hot to save anyone.

00:04:09.492 --> 00:04:13.700
Speaking of hot, I can't believe
you and Luke. You guys did it.

00:04:13.908 --> 00:04:16.492
Tell me everything.
I've been waiting for this forever.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:18.242
- You have?
- You've seen it before.

00:04:18.408 --> 00:04:19.450
- Come on!
- Touched it?

00:04:19.658 --> 00:04:22.492
Summer! It's a sacred act
between two people.

00:04:23.117 --> 00:04:26.367
It was a letdown, right?
Kind of hurt? Totally awkward?

00:04:26.575 --> 00:04:28.783
I don't have anything to compare it to.

00:04:28.992 --> 00:04:32.200
So do it again.
It is way better the second time.

00:04:32.408 --> 00:04:34.700
I'm supposed to go to his place
this afternoon.

00:04:34.908 --> 00:04:37.742
Trust me, Coop.
Get back on that horse.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:42.450
- You gotta giddyup!
- My dad's home!

00:04:42.658 --> 00:04:46.117
I don't understand. You promised me
the apartment would be ready tomorrow.

00:04:46.325 --> 00:04:50.992
Yeah, I'm moving out this weekend.
Where am I supposed to stay?

00:04:53.325 --> 00:04:57.075
Yeah, well, you don't have to apologize.
I just...

00:04:57.283 --> 00:05:00.908
You know what? Thank you.
Forget it. Yeah. Bye.

00:05:03.492 --> 00:05:05.617
- Dad?
- Hey. Hi, girls.

00:05:05.825 --> 00:05:07.825
Hey. So Summer and I are gonna go...

00:05:08.033 --> 00:05:10.908
Oh, right. You're going to
Palm Springs, yeah.

00:05:11.117 --> 00:05:14.117
We're not leaving until tomorrow.
For Tijuana?

00:05:14.325 --> 00:05:18.033
Oh, right, yeah.
Yeah, I meant... Yeah.

00:05:18.242 --> 00:05:19.492
Are you okay?

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.450
Because, I mean,
I was gonna go over to Luke's.

00:05:22.658 --> 00:05:26.992
- But if you want, I could stay here.
- No, I'm fine, sweetie. Go to Luke's.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:31.367
Luke's great. Isn't he, Summer?
He's... He's a good kid.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:33.992
Sure.

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.825
Anyway, l... I gotta... You know...

00:05:39.033 --> 00:05:40.867
Right. I know. Yeah.

00:05:41.617 --> 00:05:43.408
Okay.

00:05:43.825 --> 00:05:45.617
All right. Bye.

00:05:45.825 --> 00:05:47.658
- See you.
- See you.

00:05:58.075 --> 00:05:59.533
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.075
Is now a bad time?

00:06:02.992 --> 00:06:06.075
I don't know why you didn't come
to me in the first place.

00:06:06.283 --> 00:06:10.408
I'll call my realtor, Gloria. I'm sure
she'll be able to help you find something.

00:06:10.617 --> 00:06:12.783
Thanks. Yeah, really, thank you.

00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:16.992
So how'd the girls take the news?

00:06:18.158 --> 00:06:23.742
Well, Julie and I decided to table
that conversation until Monday.

00:06:23.908 --> 00:06:25.450
You haven't told them yet?

00:06:25.658 --> 00:06:29.617
Well, Julie's at her mom's with Kaitlin and
Marissa's going to Mexico this weekend.

00:06:29.825 --> 00:06:33.367
We just thought it'd be easier
and cleaner if we did it that way.

00:06:33.575 --> 00:06:37.700
They come back,
I'm gone, and then we tell them.

00:06:37.908 --> 00:06:39.992
I'm not so sure about this.

00:06:40.200 --> 00:06:43.825
Well, neither am I...

00:06:44.033 --> 00:06:49.533
...but the thought of having them
watch me move out...

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:53.575
It's hard enough as it is.

00:06:54.867 --> 00:06:58.033
I never thought I'd be that guy that...

00:07:00.533 --> 00:07:02.492
The divorced guy.

00:07:20.367 --> 00:07:24.283
I can't wait to go to Tijuana.
It's gonna be so romantic.

00:07:24.492 --> 00:07:26.700
It's kind of gross there.

00:07:26.908 --> 00:07:29.742
So what?
We won't leave the hotel room.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:35.367
I don't know.

00:07:38.825 --> 00:07:41.117
It'll be way better the second time.

00:07:41.325 --> 00:07:44.658
No, I mean, I don't know about Mexico.

00:07:44.867 --> 00:07:46.325
TJ.

00:07:49.742 --> 00:07:51.783
I don't think I'm gonna go.

00:07:51.992 --> 00:07:54.533
I feel like my dad's having a meltdown.

00:07:55.575 --> 00:07:59.700
You're thinking about your dad
right now? Come on, babe.

00:08:00.617 --> 00:08:03.367
I don't know if I can leave him alone.

00:08:04.867 --> 00:08:07.117
Marissa, he's, like, 40.

00:08:07.325 --> 00:08:10.533
Look, we can go to Mexico whenever.

00:08:10.742 --> 00:08:13.742
I feel like I should be with him
right now.

00:08:15.283 --> 00:08:16.867
Okay, fine.

00:08:18.033 --> 00:08:20.242
I gotta go meet the guys anyway.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.658
Is she looking at me?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.992
- Still not.
- You know what she's doing?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:40.575
And it's textbook.

00:08:40.783 --> 00:08:43.700
She's playing me hot and cold,
pretending our kiss didn't happen.

00:08:43.908 --> 00:08:46.367
There were no witnesses.
I didn't see anything.

00:08:46.575 --> 00:08:49.783
Then maybe I'll just have to make
magic happen again, won't I?

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:56.325
Hey.

00:08:58.117 --> 00:09:00.158
How you been?
I haven't seen you in a while.

00:09:00.367 --> 00:09:03.825
Yeah, well, the last time I saw you,
you kind of had your hands full.

00:09:04.700 --> 00:09:05.992
Coop! Come on.

00:09:06.242 --> 00:09:08.033
- Well, don't let me keep you.
- I won't.

00:09:08.242 --> 00:09:09.867
- Okay. Later.
- Fine.

00:09:15.742 --> 00:09:18.742
- Hey, Coop.
- Hey, Holl.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.700
You don't make those freshmen
watch a real donkey show, do you?

00:09:28.075 --> 00:09:31.408
Sandy Cohen.
How'd you get past security?

00:09:31.617 --> 00:09:33.367
- How are you, Rachel?
- Hi.

00:09:37.867 --> 00:09:41.367
You look great. Being a slave
to the Man agrees with you.

00:09:41.575 --> 00:09:45.033
Six seconds until the first insult.
You're getting soft. Still surfing?

00:09:45.242 --> 00:09:49.283
Every morning. Keeps my mind clear.
That and not working in a joint like this.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.367
Yeah. Decent hours,
appropriate compensation.

00:09:52.575 --> 00:09:54.908
I don't know how I ever left
the DA's office.

00:09:55.117 --> 00:09:58.867
It's because you kept losing
to this roguish, brilliant...

00:09:59.075 --> 00:10:02.492
- Conceited.
- That's right, it was me.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.200
What do the good folks at Partridge,
Savage and Kahn want with a lowly PD?

00:10:06.408 --> 00:10:09.408
I gotta tell you, you made some noise
with that Jimmy Cooper case.

00:10:09.617 --> 00:10:13.158
- I didn't do anything.
- You have your work cut out for you.

00:10:13.367 --> 00:10:16.867
But heading the feds off at the pass,
negotiating a restitution deal...

00:10:17.075 --> 00:10:20.450
...calling in a high-powered securities
attorney in the span of a weekend.

00:10:20.658 --> 00:10:23.242
- God, I am impressive.
- And conceited.

00:10:23.450 --> 00:10:24.825
So you keep saying.

00:10:24.992 --> 00:10:27.533
Truth be told,
no one was gonna touch that guy.

00:10:27.742 --> 00:10:31.200
The fact that you did made
the partners think, made me think.

00:10:31.408 --> 00:10:34.867
"Is Sandy Cohen really ready
to come down off his high horse?

00:10:35.075 --> 00:10:36.950
Is he finally tired of being a martyr?"

00:10:37.158 --> 00:10:39.200
Jeez, I was just hoping for a free meal.

00:10:39.408 --> 00:10:43.117
Sorry to disappoint you. All you're
getting is a really good sales pitch.

00:10:43.325 --> 00:10:45.242
Sounds delicious.

00:10:50.325 --> 00:10:51.533
What are you...?

00:10:53.075 --> 00:10:56.867
Eavesdropping, Ryan.
I hear like a wolf.

00:10:57.075 --> 00:11:00.992
- What do you mean, you're not going?
- I just... I don't know, Summ. I can't.

00:11:01.492 --> 00:11:03.200
But how am I supposed to get there?

00:11:03.408 --> 00:11:06.325
The guys are going tonight
for that stupid freshman hazing.

00:11:06.492 --> 00:11:08.867
- Holly's car is full.
- I'm sorry.

00:11:09.075 --> 00:11:11.908
I'm totally stranded.

00:11:12.075 --> 00:11:14.742
What happens in Mexico
stays in Mexico.

00:11:14.908 --> 00:11:19.200
Holly, I can't. Me and Marissa,
we're back together.

00:11:20.658 --> 00:11:24.033
I give it a week. You'll miss me.

00:11:33.575 --> 00:11:37.700
Come on, babe. Let's get you
out of here before the road trip starts.

00:11:46.492 --> 00:11:48.658
I don't know. Whatever.

00:11:48.867 --> 00:11:53.408
Hello, Summer. Seth Cohen.
I believe you remember.

00:11:56.242 --> 00:11:59.200
Nothing?
I heard you needed a ride tomorrow.

00:12:01.617 --> 00:12:04.200
- You have all our numbers.
- Dad, I know our phone number.

00:12:04.408 --> 00:12:07.617
Did you bring enough water?
Extra batteries?

00:12:07.825 --> 00:12:09.867
Air in the tires? Gas in the tank?

00:12:10.075 --> 00:12:12.408
It's amazing I turned out so normal.

00:12:13.408 --> 00:12:16.242
Hey. Let me get that.

00:12:19.908 --> 00:12:22.825
Hey, Summer. Sandy Cohen.
I'm Seth's dad.

00:12:23.033 --> 00:12:25.033
I had no idea you were
into comic books.

00:12:25.242 --> 00:12:26.867
Comic books?

00:12:27.075 --> 00:12:29.533
- She goes for the anime.
- Anime.

00:12:29.742 --> 00:12:32.742
I'm gonna go say bye to Coop.
Don't touch my stuff.

00:12:35.408 --> 00:12:37.033
This is gonna be awesome.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:38.575
She is hot stuff, son.

00:12:38.783 --> 00:12:40.867
And now it's ruined.

00:12:41.075 --> 00:12:44.908
- I told you, I can't go.
- I got us a ride. Just grab some stuff.

00:12:45.117 --> 00:12:48.033
Hey. What are you guys
still doing here?

00:12:48.242 --> 00:12:49.908
I thought I'd stay home this weekend.

00:12:50.117 --> 00:12:52.867
What? Why? I thought you were
looking forward to this trip.

00:12:53.033 --> 00:12:56.200
I was. But I thought maybe
we could spend some time together.

00:12:56.408 --> 00:12:59.075
Well, we can't, I'm sorry.

00:12:59.242 --> 00:13:02.992
I thought you were going,
so I made other plans.

00:13:03.658 --> 00:13:06.408
I was. I just...

00:13:06.617 --> 00:13:08.242
I mean, are you sure?

00:13:09.242 --> 00:13:12.117
- Because I thought maybe we could...
- Look, Marissa, please.

00:13:12.325 --> 00:13:15.075
Come on.
I can't take care of both of us.

00:13:16.992 --> 00:13:19.742
Okay. I'll go pack my stuff.

00:13:21.908 --> 00:13:23.283
Coop?

00:13:26.908 --> 00:13:29.367
- So who's going with us?
- You'll see.

00:13:30.742 --> 00:13:34.367
Great news. I got Coop to come along.

00:13:46.575 --> 00:13:48.367
We're going to TJ!

00:13:55.908 --> 00:13:58.742
I can't believe you convinced me
to do this.

00:13:58.908 --> 00:14:02.158
- You could've brought somebody in.
- Where's the fun in that?

00:14:02.367 --> 00:14:05.367
It only took us a couple of hours
to paint my dorm room, remember?

00:14:05.575 --> 00:14:07.992
Your dorm room was the size
of a prison cell.

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.283
Well, we may be painting
one of those as well.

00:14:11.492 --> 00:14:12.742
Sorry.

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:14.867
Listen, thank you so much.

00:14:15.075 --> 00:14:18.867
The thought of being home
when Julie and the kids come back...

00:14:19.075 --> 00:14:21.742
- You haven't told them yet.
- Well, not exactly.

00:14:21.908 --> 00:14:26.658
I mean, I was gonna tell Marissa,
but then it just seemed impossibly hard.

00:14:26.867 --> 00:14:29.867
Because it is.
Jimmy, Marissa's not a little girl anymore.

00:14:30.075 --> 00:14:34.450
And if she comes home and finds
you gone, she'll never forgive you.

00:14:37.825 --> 00:14:39.825
Call her.

00:14:40.033 --> 00:14:43.200
She'll still love you. I promise.

00:14:47.075 --> 00:14:48.867
We should be there in three hours.

00:14:49.075 --> 00:14:51.075
The GPS says the ETA's
three and a half.

00:14:51.283 --> 00:14:54.200
Well, that's because someone drives
like an old woman.

00:14:54.408 --> 00:14:56.200
I'm going 70 in a 65 zone.

00:14:56.408 --> 00:14:57.867
Eighty is the new 70.

00:14:58.033 --> 00:15:00.117
What? Who talks like that?

00:15:00.325 --> 00:15:03.242
Who gets passed by a van full of nuns?

00:15:03.408 --> 00:15:04.867
Oh, wait, Cohen does.

00:15:05.075 --> 00:15:07.908
They have God on their side.
I'm not gonna beat Jesus.

00:15:08.075 --> 00:15:10.283
I'm gonna call Holly
and see how far ahead she is.

00:15:10.492 --> 00:15:13.408
- And she's a girl.
- That's insulting to your own gender.

00:15:13.617 --> 00:15:17.242
- Not as insulting as it is to you.
- Point taken.

00:15:20.283 --> 00:15:21.742
No, thanks.

00:15:22.325 --> 00:15:23.867
I'll take it.

00:15:24.075 --> 00:15:25.658
I'm so dehydrated.

00:15:25.867 --> 00:15:29.992
What is up with the a.c.? My hair
is frizzing out. I look like Howard Stern.

00:15:30.158 --> 00:15:34.908
- My Jewfro benefits from this climate.
- You're Jewish?

00:15:35.575 --> 00:15:38.408
Yes. That's why I feel so comfortable
in this desert heat.

00:15:38.617 --> 00:15:42.950
This is a nightmare. I'm sweating
to death, driving 10 miles an hour...

00:15:43.158 --> 00:15:45.533
...in, like, a rickshaw,
listening to this music.

00:15:45.908 --> 00:15:47.867
Hey, do not insult Death Cab.

00:15:48.075 --> 00:15:50.533
It's, like, one guitar
and a whole lot of complaining.

00:15:50.742 --> 00:15:53.825
Reminds me of someone else
who's doing a lot of complaining. You.

00:15:54.033 --> 00:15:58.700
I'm driving this vehicle, and I'll drive
at the speed that I feel comfortable, okay?

00:15:58.908 --> 00:16:00.533
It's my music, it is my snacks...

00:16:00.742 --> 00:16:02.700
Kudos and Goldfish? What are you, 8?

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.200
- Say goodbye to Summer.
- What are you doing?

00:16:05.408 --> 00:16:08.242
Leaving you at the side of the road.
Don't touch the wheel!

00:16:08.408 --> 00:16:11.075
Stop! Stop it!

00:16:11.242 --> 00:16:13.700
- Guys, stop it!
- Seth!

00:16:28.992 --> 00:16:31.033
It's not exactly the honeymoon suite.

00:16:31.242 --> 00:16:33.992
Well, it's only for one night,
until the axle's fixed.

00:16:34.158 --> 00:16:37.325
- I've stayed in worse.
- That's nothing to brag about.

00:16:37.533 --> 00:16:42.033
Sweet!
Do we have to pay extra for the pubes?

00:16:42.242 --> 00:16:46.617
- This is so gross. I cannot stay here.
- Unless you feel like hitchhiking again...

00:16:46.825 --> 00:16:50.200
No, thank you. I've spent
enough time in a truck full of chickens.

00:16:50.408 --> 00:16:52.117
Hey, we're lucky that guy stopped.

00:16:52.283 --> 00:16:55.575
We'd be even luckier if Cole Trickle here
hadn't driven us off the road.

00:16:55.783 --> 00:16:59.033
- Who the hell is Cole Trickle?
- Tom Cruise. Days of Thunder.

00:16:59.242 --> 00:17:00.867
Guys, can we try to be positive?

00:17:01.075 --> 00:17:03.075
Okay. I am positive this is Summer's fault.

00:17:03.283 --> 00:17:05.408
I'm positive that I'm leaving
here with a rash.

00:17:05.617 --> 00:17:08.700
Oh, so you plan on making
some extra money tonight.

00:17:12.533 --> 00:17:16.158
This bathroom is so...

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:22.450
- Hello.
- Hey.

00:17:22.658 --> 00:17:25.700
Hey, what happened to you?
You're finger-painting in the back yard?

00:17:25.908 --> 00:17:28.408
I was helping Jimmy
paint his new living room.

00:17:28.617 --> 00:17:32.825
- Julie kicked him out?
- Is that okay that I'm helping him?

00:17:33.033 --> 00:17:35.700
Yeah, I guess, with everything
he's been going through.

00:17:35.908 --> 00:17:38.367
Honey! You shouldn't have!

00:17:38.575 --> 00:17:42.325
I didn't. It washed up
about an hour ago. Who's Rachel?

00:17:42.533 --> 00:17:44.367
She works at the law firm I met with.

00:17:44.575 --> 00:17:47.075
Well, the meeting must have gone well.
You never said.

00:17:47.283 --> 00:17:49.283
You must have let them down easy.

00:17:49.492 --> 00:17:53.158
In a private practice, I could do more
pro bono work than I do now.

00:17:53.367 --> 00:17:57.867
Sandy, you're not seriously considering
taking this job, are you?

00:17:58.075 --> 00:18:00.533
The salary they offered me
is outrageous.

00:18:00.742 --> 00:18:05.450
You've never been swayed by a paycheck.
This family has all the money it needs.

00:18:05.658 --> 00:18:06.867
Except it's your money.

00:18:07.075 --> 00:18:08.700
- It's our money.
- Not really.

00:18:08.908 --> 00:18:11.575
Unless you wanna buy the Lakers
or a Caribbean island.

00:18:11.783 --> 00:18:14.533
It's not about buying stuff,
although Aruba would be nice.

00:18:14.742 --> 00:18:17.658
It's about contributing.
And I have an opportunity here.

00:18:18.325 --> 00:18:20.492
Yeah, to work for people
that you hate.

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.158
You refer to those places as...

00:18:22.325 --> 00:18:25.658
...evil empires controlled by
corporate interests, owned by the Man.

00:18:25.867 --> 00:18:29.200
Well, I tend to be hyperbolic.
It goes with the territory.

00:18:29.408 --> 00:18:31.408
The PD office is your life.

00:18:31.617 --> 00:18:34.908
I don't want you to give that up
so you can buy groceries the next week.

00:18:35.117 --> 00:18:38.325
Don't belittle this.
I think balance is important.

00:18:38.533 --> 00:18:40.700
- We don't have balance?
- No, you have all the money.

00:18:40.908 --> 00:18:43.450
And you have all the ideals.

00:18:43.658 --> 00:18:46.075
- You like that I don't make a lot of money.
- What?

00:18:46.283 --> 00:18:50.575
It makes us different from all these
other families. All these other women...

00:18:50.783 --> 00:18:53.908
...married to their investment bankers
and their CEOs.

00:18:54.117 --> 00:18:56.700
As long as I haven't sold out,
you haven't sold out.

00:18:56.908 --> 00:18:58.742
- That's not true.
- Come on, face it.

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:03.158
The only thing that keeps you
from feeling like Julie Cooper is me.

00:19:05.867 --> 00:19:08.617
But, hey, it's just an offer.

00:19:12.408 --> 00:19:15.533
I have to pick wisely.
Ding Dongs or Cheese Sticks?

00:19:15.742 --> 00:19:17.617
I don't care. Pick whatever.

00:19:17.825 --> 00:19:21.242
- I don't care either.
- So I guess we'll just starve.

00:19:24.200 --> 00:19:27.033
- You ever gonna stop being mad at me?
- I'm not mad at you.

00:19:27.242 --> 00:19:28.825
Right.

00:19:29.992 --> 00:19:33.242
- Why would I be mad at you?
- You walked in on me with another girl.

00:19:33.450 --> 00:19:36.867
Actually, I think she was a woman.
But why would I care about that?

00:19:37.075 --> 00:19:40.658
- I don't know. Shouldn't be a problem.
- There's no problem.

00:19:40.867 --> 00:19:43.367
Except Ding Dongs or Cheese Sticks.

00:19:44.033 --> 00:19:45.200
I don't care, Ryan.

00:19:45.408 --> 00:19:48.533
I don't care about Cheese Sticks
and I don't care about Ding Dongs.

00:19:48.742 --> 00:19:52.700
And I really don't care that I walked
in on you with some girl. Or woman.

00:19:52.908 --> 00:19:54.700
Whatever.

00:19:56.908 --> 00:20:00.408
I was only with her because
you were clearly back with Luke.

00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:02.242
I was not back with Luke.

00:20:04.242 --> 00:20:05.492
You are now, right?

00:20:06.408 --> 00:20:08.617
- Right.
- Okay.

00:20:08.825 --> 00:20:12.533
Great. So we'll just get to Mexico,
split up and never talk again.

00:20:12.742 --> 00:20:14.700
Sounds like a plan.

00:20:16.992 --> 00:20:18.867
By the way,
you could have knocked first.

00:20:20.075 --> 00:20:23.075
Did you ever wonder why
I came to the pool house to find you?

00:20:23.742 --> 00:20:25.117
Every day.

00:20:27.533 --> 00:20:30.700
Here's your chance.
Clear the air. Tell me.

00:20:38.492 --> 00:20:41.325
Cheese Sticks. I hate Ding Dongs.

00:20:44.575 --> 00:20:46.367
Hey. Static.

00:20:46.575 --> 00:20:48.158
That's awesome.

00:20:53.950 --> 00:20:55.825
What are you doing?

00:20:56.033 --> 00:21:00.700
Almost watching TV. This is either
SpongeBob SquarePants or JAG.

00:21:00.908 --> 00:21:02.867
Get off the bed.
The sooner I go to sleep...

00:21:03.075 --> 00:21:06.700
...the sooner it'll be morning
and this nightmare will be over.

00:21:07.492 --> 00:21:11.533
I'm not sleeping on that couch. It's
stained and smells foul. You sleep there.

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:14.158
After you've made it sound
so appealing? Good night.

00:21:14.367 --> 00:21:16.075
- Come on, get off the bed!
- Nope.

00:21:16.283 --> 00:21:19.325
- Be, like, a gentleman.
- Chivalry's dead, sugar.

00:21:28.825 --> 00:21:31.033
You make a move,
I rip out your jugular.

00:21:31.575 --> 00:21:33.033
Oh, hey, pillow talk.

00:21:59.575 --> 00:22:00.867
Hello?

00:22:01.075 --> 00:22:03.033
Oh, hey, Dad.

00:22:03.658 --> 00:22:05.492
Hey, you got a minute, kiddo?

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:08.950
Yeah. Is everything okay?

00:22:09.158 --> 00:22:11.283
Well, no.

00:22:11.492 --> 00:22:13.867
Not exactly.

00:22:17.283 --> 00:22:18.867
What is it?

00:22:20.575 --> 00:22:24.033
This isn 't a very easy thing to say.

00:22:25.450 --> 00:22:30.367
When you get home,
I'm not gonna be there.

00:22:31.325 --> 00:22:33.033
Your mom and I are...

00:22:33.242 --> 00:22:34.867
You're getting a divorce.

00:22:35.492 --> 00:22:39.033
I just can't believe you're telling me this
over the phone.

00:22:40.908 --> 00:22:46.325
I was gonna tell you before you left,
but then I knew you'd stay.

00:22:47.367 --> 00:22:50.783
And I just couldn 't let you
watch me pack up my life.

00:22:55.117 --> 00:22:58.575
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry, kiddo.

00:23:01.408 --> 00:23:04.867
I don 't wanna ruin your whole trip.
It's good that you went.

00:23:22.908 --> 00:23:24.367
I can sleep on the floor.

00:23:25.575 --> 00:23:27.033
No, it's okay.

00:23:47.033 --> 00:23:48.325
I'm sorry.

00:23:53.242 --> 00:23:54.700
Thanks.

00:25:24.908 --> 00:25:26.783
Sorry. I didn't mean to.

00:25:26.992 --> 00:25:28.533
I know.

00:25:36.700 --> 00:25:38.325
You wanna go home?

00:25:39.992 --> 00:25:41.617
I just...

00:25:43.658 --> 00:25:45.783
I think I wanna stay here.

00:25:50.492 --> 00:25:52.617
I'm gonna go take a shower.

00:26:22.533 --> 00:26:24.158
So...

00:26:24.325 --> 00:26:26.450
...Tijuana.
- Yeah.

00:26:26.992 --> 00:26:28.617
Should we have woke Ryan
and Marissa?

00:26:28.825 --> 00:26:32.075
No. They looked so cute together.
Vomit.

00:26:32.283 --> 00:26:35.117
Hey. That's a real sentimental streak
you got there, Summer.

00:26:35.325 --> 00:26:37.742
It's too early for your so-called comedy.

00:26:37.950 --> 00:26:39.492
You enjoy my comedy.

00:26:41.783 --> 00:26:44.700
You know what else I think you enjoy?
Me.

00:26:44.908 --> 00:26:46.825
That's because you're mentally unstable.

00:26:47.033 --> 00:26:49.367
Be that as it may,
the facts speak for themselves.

00:26:49.575 --> 00:26:52.033
Might I remind you of something
that I call...

00:26:52.242 --> 00:26:55.367
..."the time that you kissed me
at my grandfather's party."

00:26:55.575 --> 00:26:57.200
- What are you talking about?
- Okay.

00:26:57.408 --> 00:27:00.242
I know that denial is a very powerful
coping mechanism...

00:27:00.408 --> 00:27:03.492
...but it's time we paid lip service
to our lip service.

00:27:03.700 --> 00:27:06.783
Two words: No tongue.

00:27:06.992 --> 00:27:11.117
- You agreed to take this trip with me.
- I needed a ride.

00:27:11.325 --> 00:27:12.700
We shared the same bed.

00:27:12.908 --> 00:27:15.158
I wasn't sleeping on that couch.
It smelled like eggs.

00:27:15.367 --> 00:27:18.492
- You ate my toast, Summer.
- I like crusts, Seth.

00:27:18.700 --> 00:27:21.283
Face it. Our chemistry is undeniable.

00:27:21.742 --> 00:27:24.117
- You know what else is undeniable?
- What?

00:27:24.325 --> 00:27:28.367
The pain this fork is gonna cause
when I jam it into your eye.

00:27:30.825 --> 00:27:32.825
I suffer from rage blackouts.

00:27:33.408 --> 00:27:35.617
I'm gonna get the check.

00:27:39.158 --> 00:27:40.325
Where's Coop?

00:27:40.533 --> 00:27:43.033
- The shower.
- Hope she's wearing shower shoes.

00:27:43.242 --> 00:27:46.575
Here's breakfast, and the chariot's
repaired and out front. Ready to go?

00:27:46.783 --> 00:27:49.075
- I'm not sure we're going.
- What?

00:27:51.408 --> 00:27:54.408
Marissa's dad called
with some bad news.

00:27:56.450 --> 00:27:58.408
What's going on?

00:28:00.825 --> 00:28:03.825
They're getting divorced.

00:28:04.033 --> 00:28:06.700
Baby, I'm so sorry.

00:28:09.825 --> 00:28:11.367
Whatever you wanna do, Coop.

00:28:11.575 --> 00:28:14.242
But if I may,
speaking as a child of divorce...

00:28:14.408 --> 00:28:16.450
...you do not wanna be home
right now.

00:28:16.908 --> 00:28:18.950
And this is our last chance for freedom.

00:28:19.158 --> 00:28:21.742
We get back to Newport,
and it's school and reality.

00:28:21.950 --> 00:28:26.450
Let's go to TJ, have fun.
Life will suck soon enough.

00:28:27.658 --> 00:28:30.325
She might actually be right.

00:28:30.492 --> 00:28:32.825
Well, there's a first time for everything.

00:28:33.408 --> 00:28:35.408
Rage blackouts, got it. I'll be in the car.

00:28:40.742 --> 00:28:42.492
Let's go to TJ.

00:28:58.908 --> 00:29:02.117
I still don't understand
why we needed to get two rooms.

00:29:02.325 --> 00:29:04.617
I'll leave you my key
just in case you get Ionely.

00:29:04.825 --> 00:29:07.908
Or in case I wanna smother you
with your pillow.

00:29:08.075 --> 00:29:10.908
- Whatever turns you on.
- Everyone's at Boom-Boom.

00:29:11.075 --> 00:29:14.450
I have to go to the pharmacy. You can
get anything without a prescription.

00:29:14.658 --> 00:29:16.492
I need to make a pit stop
for my stepmom.

00:29:16.700 --> 00:29:19.617
She's taken all the painkillers
available in Orange County.

00:29:19.825 --> 00:29:23.658
I should probably pop in and pick up
an antihistamine. Allergies.

00:29:24.992 --> 00:29:27.908
You don't have to come with us
if you don't want.

00:29:28.117 --> 00:29:29.992
I'm going to find Luke.

00:29:30.575 --> 00:29:33.117
It's okay. Really. That's fine.

00:29:39.158 --> 00:29:43.533
Hey, where are the partners? Oh, right,
I forgot. Vampires hate the sunlight.

00:29:43.742 --> 00:29:46.867
- They didn't want to appear desperate.
- So they sent you.

00:29:47.075 --> 00:29:51.033
- Desperation's your strong suit.
- And yours is...

00:29:51.242 --> 00:29:53.908
I'm drawing a blank here.

00:29:54.075 --> 00:29:57.867
They're pulling the offer first thing in
the morning unless they hear from you.

00:29:58.075 --> 00:30:01.908
Thank them for the surfboard,
although it did freak my wife out.

00:30:02.117 --> 00:30:04.533
You had her believing
I was considering this job.

00:30:04.742 --> 00:30:06.658
- Which you are.
- No.

00:30:06.867 --> 00:30:10.700
As much as I'd like to think you're here
for the sparkling banter and crab cakes...

00:30:10.908 --> 00:30:12.158
...I know you're interested.

00:30:12.367 --> 00:30:17.158
It's not gonna happen. I've been in the
PD's office my whole life. It's what I do.

00:30:17.367 --> 00:30:19.492
And I'm giving you
a platform to do it better.

00:30:19.700 --> 00:30:21.325
The sand dabs are great here.

00:30:21.533 --> 00:30:24.283
Don't you wanna see what
would happen if you tested yourself?

00:30:24.492 --> 00:30:27.242
Not just against one more overworked,
underpaid ADA.

00:30:27.450 --> 00:30:29.242
I always loved beating you.

00:30:29.450 --> 00:30:31.533
- You know why?
- Why?

00:30:31.742 --> 00:30:33.283
Because I was excellent.

00:30:34.825 --> 00:30:38.117
Which is why I left.
I wanted to do more.

00:30:38.325 --> 00:30:39.700
And so do you.

00:30:40.992 --> 00:30:42.617
The clock's ticking.

00:30:44.408 --> 00:30:45.950
Sand dabs, huh?

00:30:46.117 --> 00:30:47.492
Yep.

00:30:48.575 --> 00:30:51.658
Of course she would be.
But telling her...

00:30:51.825 --> 00:30:53.450
You were totally right.

00:30:53.658 --> 00:30:55.200
It'll take a while.

00:30:55.367 --> 00:30:59.242
It's gonna take us all
a while to get used to this.

00:30:59.450 --> 00:31:02.117
My swinging new bachelor pad.

00:31:04.158 --> 00:31:07.325
You know, this is the first time
I've ever really been a bachelor.

00:31:07.533 --> 00:31:12.617
I mean, I went from you to Julie,
and the rest is...

00:31:15.075 --> 00:31:16.950
Let me ask you something.

00:31:17.158 --> 00:31:22.658
You ever have any doubts
about you and Sandy?

00:31:22.825 --> 00:31:24.783
We have our issues.

00:31:26.117 --> 00:31:29.992
You ever think what it would be like
if you and I had ended up...?

00:31:31.492 --> 00:31:32.867
Sometimes.

00:31:35.533 --> 00:31:36.908
Finished.

00:31:56.658 --> 00:31:58.575
I should go.

00:31:58.783 --> 00:32:02.367
Yeah, I'm sorry, that was totally...
That was wrong of me.

00:32:02.575 --> 00:32:06.450
My marriage is falling apart,
but I shouldn't try to bring yours down.

00:32:06.658 --> 00:32:09.700
- I'm gonna go.
- Okay. I'm sorry. L...

00:32:51.408 --> 00:32:56.242
- Come on, Luke. Back that ass up.
- No, that's cool.

00:32:57.158 --> 00:32:58.367
Marissa's not even coming.

00:33:00.992 --> 00:33:02.867
Come on. I love this song.

00:33:17.825 --> 00:33:21.492
I love authentic Mexican culture.

00:34:32.533 --> 00:34:35.200
- What are you doing?
- I didn't know. I'm sorry.

00:34:35.408 --> 00:34:36.992
What, that you got caught?

00:34:37.200 --> 00:34:40.867
- Don't ever talk to me again.
- You are such a bitch.

00:34:41.075 --> 00:34:43.742
- Please. He hooks up with everyone.
- Shut up.

00:34:43.908 --> 00:34:47.533
Freshman girls,
girls from Mater Dei, girls from UCI.

00:34:47.742 --> 00:34:49.283
Is that true?

00:34:49.992 --> 00:34:54.408
Marissa, everyone knows. Everyone!
Now you do too.

00:34:55.158 --> 00:34:57.742
- You are so mean.
- Summer, I am honest.

00:34:58.408 --> 00:35:01.408
Her parents are getting divorced,
you stupid slut!

00:35:01.617 --> 00:35:04.783
Walk away, Holly.
She suffers from rage blackouts.

00:35:05.075 --> 00:35:06.617
- Let her go.
- This isn't about you.

00:35:06.825 --> 00:35:08.533
- It is now.
- Get out of my way.

00:35:08.742 --> 00:35:10.450
You don't deserve her.

00:35:22.492 --> 00:35:25.242
- I'll go check the hotel.
- I'll check the streets.

00:35:25.408 --> 00:35:27.158
Call me if you find her.

00:35:41.908 --> 00:35:44.033
Thank God, Coop.

00:35:49.533 --> 00:35:52.408
I slept with him.

00:35:52.617 --> 00:35:54.408
I know, sweetie.

00:35:57.575 --> 00:36:01.950
- I gotta call Ryan and Seth.
- No. I don't wanna see them.

00:36:02.117 --> 00:36:03.742
Just...

00:36:03.950 --> 00:36:05.825
I'm so embarrassed.

00:36:06.033 --> 00:36:10.242
It's okay. It's just...
We'll go home.

00:36:11.408 --> 00:36:14.908
I can't go home. My dad will be gone.

00:36:15.117 --> 00:36:18.408
My mom's gonna be back. I have...

00:36:19.575 --> 00:36:21.367
I have no one.

00:36:24.200 --> 00:36:26.658
Come on, Coop. Let's get out of here.

00:36:31.908 --> 00:36:34.033
I'll grab our stuff.

00:36:53.658 --> 00:36:54.950
Hey, it's me.

00:36:55.158 --> 00:36:56.617
Hey.

00:36:56.825 --> 00:36:58.908
- I found her.
- You did?

00:36:59.117 --> 00:37:00.658
She's at the hotel.

00:37:00.825 --> 00:37:02.742
- You guys need to get here fast.
- Okay.

00:37:02.950 --> 00:37:04.575
Okay.

00:37:06.492 --> 00:37:09.658
Hey, Coop.
You wanna get some dinner?

00:37:09.867 --> 00:37:11.783
What are you in the mood for?

00:37:13.117 --> 00:37:14.825
Coop?

00:37:16.158 --> 00:37:17.367
Coop.

00:37:24.117 --> 00:37:25.658
Okay.

00:37:26.783 --> 00:37:28.700
- Bad news. She's gone.
- What?

00:37:29.242 --> 00:37:30.908
And so are my stepmom's painkillers.

00:37:32.742 --> 00:37:36.200
- Should we split up?
- No, let's stick together. Come on.

00:38:42.075 --> 00:38:43.533
- Hey.
- Hey.

00:38:44.158 --> 00:38:45.700
How'd it go with the suits?

00:38:45.867 --> 00:38:47.700
You know, okay.

00:38:50.325 --> 00:38:52.117
I can't believe summer's over.

00:38:52.325 --> 00:38:53.950
I know.

00:38:54.158 --> 00:38:57.617
Feels like it goes faster and faster
every year.

00:38:59.158 --> 00:39:01.992
So if I did take this job...

00:39:02.200 --> 00:39:04.867
You've already taken it.

00:39:05.367 --> 00:39:06.825
Haven't you?

00:39:07.033 --> 00:39:09.908
I can still get out of it if you want me to.

00:39:19.367 --> 00:39:21.408
To a new season.

00:40:36.408 --> 00:40:37.867
Coop!

00:40:39.242 --> 00:40:40.950
Coop!

00:42:02.783 --> 00:42:04.408
Hey, honey, come on.

00:42:06.242 --> 00:42:08.033
Wake up.

00:42:08.242 --> 00:42:10.033
Wake up.
